export const str REGISTRY_SRC =
    "# CobaltC Diagnostic Registry\n\nStatus: normative artifact\nVersion: 1.62.0\nConforms to: `spec/02-sche"
    "ma.md` (Kind: Diagnostic, `diag.<name>`)\nGoverned by: `CobaltC_Master_Instructions.md` §19\n\n## Purp"
    "ose\n\nEvery `diag.*` id any rule produces, with the fields §19 requires.\nEvery entry has **Status:**"
    " ACCEPTED. Conventions: **Phase** is\n*static* (a `disposition: rejected` rule, or a `checked` rule w"
    "hose\nguard `rule.control.flow-analysis` refuted), *dynamic* (a `checked`\nrule's runtime guard), or *"
    "both*. **Summary** is the diagnostic's\nmessage when its occurrence gives none of its own. **Location"
    "** is,\nunless stated, the expression the triggering rule's premises were\nevaluated against; it is a "
    "file, a line and a column, the column being\nthat of the location's first token, counted in character"
    "s from 1 (a\nlocation that is a declaration or a statement is its first token).\n**Related** cites `ex"
    ".*` (`spec/examples.md`). When a program has\nseveral static errors, the one reported is the first in"
    " the source (the\nlowest line; among one line's errors, any), whatever order a checker\nvisits the pro"
    "gram in (`CHG-0130`).\n\n**How a diagnostic is shown** (D-0228). Both implementations print every\ndiag"
    "nostic in the same form, byte for byte. By default it is short: a first\nline `error[diag.x]: message"
    "` for a static diagnostic or `fault[diag.x]:\nmessage` for a dynamic one, where the message is the oc"
    "currence's own or\nthe entry's **Summary**; then `--> file:line:column`; then the source line,\nread f"
    "rom the file when the diagnostic is shown, with carets under the\nlocation's token; then `= repair:` "
    "and the entry's **Repair**. A file\nthat cannot be read is shown as its location alone. With `--expla"
    "in`\n(both tools), or with `COBALTC_EXPLAIN` set to anything but empty or `0`\n(this is how a compiled"
    " program is asked), the entry's Rule, Invariant,\nRequired, Observed and Provenance follow, then its "
    "Related examples and\nthis registry. A conformance case requires the id and the phase\n(`spec/conforma"
    "nce.md`), which a runner reads from the first line's\nopening `error[diag.ID]` or `fault[diag.ID]` (`"
    "impl/conformance/run.py`);\nthe location is as this registry gives it; the rest of the form's\nwording"
    " is not normative.\n\n## Syntax\n\n- `diag.syntax-error` — Summary: the text is not a CobaltC program "
    "here. Phase: static. Rule: the grammar, `spec/22` (lexical §1, syntactic §2–§3, and each rule t"
    "hat makes a form a syntax error, such as `[Slice-Not-Borrowed]`). Invariant: none. Required: the tex"
    "t is a CobaltC program by the grammar. Observed: at the location, the first token (or character) whe"
    "re the grammar allows none of what the message says was expected; nothing of the program runs. Prove"
    "nance: the source text. Repair: correct the text there; the message names what was expected and what"
    " was found. Location: that token.\n\n## Names and scoping\n\n- `diag.unbound-name` — Summary: this nam"
    "e is not declared. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.value-object.binding-lookup` `[Binding-Lookup-Unbound]"
    "`, `rule.module.resolve` `[Resolve-Unbound]`, `spec/21` §0 `fault`'s name (D-0083). Invariant: none"
    ". Required: the name resolves to a binding or item. Observed: it does not. Provenance: use site vs. "
    "every declaration in scope. Repair: declare it, fix the spelling, or add an `import` (`import std;` "
    "for the standard library, `CHG-0033`). Related: `ex.unbound-name`.\n- `diag.ambiguous-name` — Summa"
    "ry: this name could mean more than one item. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.resolve` `[Resolve-Am"
    "biguous]`. Required: exactly one candidate. Observed: several (two `import`s, two imported modules e"
    "xporting the name, two enums of the same module with the variant, or, where no module of the program"
    "'s own has it, two imported enums with it). Provenance: the candidate declarations. Repair: qualify "
    "the name.\n- `diag.name-not-visible` — Summary: this item is private to its module. Phase: static. "
    "Rule: `rule.module.resolve` `[Resolve-Not-Visible]`; `rule.module.visibility` `[Field-Not-Visible]` "
    "(a field named by `e.f`, a struct literal, or a destructuring). Required: `visible(M', name, M)`. Ob"
    "served: private. Provenance: the declaration's `export` marker vs. the use site's module. Repair: ma"
    "rk `export` or move the reference.\n- `diag.no-main` — Summary: the program has no `main` it can st"
    "art from. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.fn.program` `[Program-No-Main]`. Invariant: none. Required: exa"
    "ctly one non-generic, non-`extern` `main` at the root module, with no parameters, returning `void` o"
    "r `u8`. Observed: none there (a `main` inside a module is the ordinary item `m::main`), or one with "
    "parameters, another return type, type parameters, or `extern`. Provenance: the root module's items. "
    "Repair: declare `fn main()` or `fn main() : u8` at the root (arguments come from `arg`, `spec/21` §"
    "2c), or run the file that has one — a file-backed module's body is not a program (`spec/17` §5). "
    "Location: the root `main`, if there is one; otherwise the program as a whole.\n- `diag.const-not-cons"
    "tant` — Summary: a constant's value must be known before the program runs. Phase: static. Rule: `r"
    "ule.module.const` `[Const-Not-Constant]`, `[Const-Cycle]`, `[Const-Local-Not-Constant]` (`spec/17` §"
    "1a). Invariant: none. Required: a `const`'s type is not a resource, its initializer is a constant ex"
    "pression (literals, operators, other constants, struct, array and variant literals of constant expre"
    "ssions and their fields and elements, a function's name, the pure intrinsics listed there), and no c"
    "onstant depends on itself; a local constant's initializer names no local variable and no type parame"
    "ter of its function. Observed: one of these fails. Provenance: the `const` declaration. Repair: use "
    "only constants in the initializer (a local variable is not one, even when set from a literal: declar"
    "e it `const` too), compute the value in a function instead, or break the cycle. Location: the `const"
    "`.\n- `diag.format-invalid` — Summary: this format string is not valid. Phase: static. Rule: `rule."
    "stdlib.format` `[Format-Invalid]` (`spec/21` §2f). Invariant: none. Required: the format of `printf"
    "`, `sprintf`, `eprintf` or `String::appendf` is a string literal whose every `%` begins a specifier "
    "`%[flags][width][.precision]conversion` with a conversion of `d i u x X o b f F e E g G s v` (or is "
    "`%%`), and flags the conversion takes. Observed: a format that is not a literal, a `%` at the end, a"
    "n unknown conversion, a flag the conversion does not take (`%#d`, `%0s`, `%+x`, `%05v`), a precision"
    " on `%v`, or a width or precision above 4096. Provenance: the call. Repair: fix the specifier; write"
    " `%%` for a `%`. Location: the call.\n- `diag.module-file-not-found` — Summary: the module's file c"
    "annot be read. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.file` `[Module-File-Missing]`. Invariant: none. Req"
    "uired: the declaration's path, resolved against the declaring file's directory, names a readable fil"
    "e. Observed: it names none. Provenance: the declaration's path and the directory it was resolved aga"
    "inst. Repair: fix the path or create the file. Location: the `module` declaration.\n- `diag.module-cy"
    "cle` — Summary: these module files contain each other. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.file` `[M"
    "odule-File-Cycle]`. Invariant: none. Required: no file's body contains, directly or through further "
    "file-backed declarations, itself. Observed: a cycle `F → … → F`. Provenance: each declaration "
    "on the cycle. Repair: break the cycle — move the shared items into a third file both name. Locatio"
    "n: the declaration that closes the cycle.\n- `diag.module-file-duplicate` — Summary: this file is a"
    "lready declared as a module. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.file` `[Module-File-Duplicate]`. Inva"
    "riant: none. Required: each file is named by at most one declaration in the program. Observed: two. "
    "Provenance: both declarations. Repair: declare the module once and reach it by qualified path or `im"
    "port`. Location: the second declaration.\n- `diag.duplicate-local` — Summary: this name is already "
    "declared in this block. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.value-object.binding-form` `[Binding-Form-Redecla"
    "red]` (D-0131). Invariant: none. Required: each name is declared at most once in a declaration regio"
    "n — a block's statements with the parameters, loop names or pattern binder governing it. Observed:"
    " a second declaration (a local variable, a destructured binder, a local constant, a parameter, or a "
    "loop's or pattern's name). Provenance: both declarations (the message says how far above the first o"
    "ne is). Repair: assign to the existing variable (`x = …`, after a `drop` for a live resource), or "
    "choose another name, as when the type changes; a nested block may shadow. Location: the second decla"
    "ration.\n- `diag.duplicate-item` — Summary: this name is already declared in this module. Phase: st"
    "atic. Rule: `rule.module.resolve` `[Item-Duplicate]`. Invariant: none. Required: each qualified name"
    " — `M::name` for a `fn`, `extern fn`, `struct`, `enum` or `module`, `M::T::name` for an associated"
    " function, `M::E::V` for an enum variant — is added by at most one declaration. Observed: two. Pro"
    "venance: both declarations. Repair: rename one, or move it into a module. Location: the second decla"
    "ration.\n- `diag.foreign-associated-fn` — Summary: an associated function must be declared beside i"
    "ts type. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.resolve` `[Assoc-Fn-Foreign-Type]`. Invariant: none. Requ"
    "ired: `fn T::name` is declared in the module that declares the struct or enum `T`. Observed: `T` is "
    "declared elsewhere (for example `std`'s `Vec`) or not at all. Provenance: the declaration and `T`'s "
    "module. Repair: declare an ordinary function, or move the declaration into `T`'s module. Location: t"
    "he declaration.\n- `diag.deprecated-use` — Summary: this item is deprecated. Phase: static. Rule: `"
    "rule.module.retired` `[Use-Deprecated]` (`spec/17` §1, D-0303). Invariant: none. Required: the name"
    " used is live. Observed: its declaration is marked `[[deprecated(\"m\")]]`, or its module's or its typ"
    "e's is. Provenance: the use, and the declaration that carries the attribute. Repair: write what the "
    "message says instead; meanwhile `--allow-deprecated` accepts the program and reports each use as a w"
    "arning. Related: `ex.deprecated-use`.\n- `diag.removed-use` — Summary: this item was removed. Phase"
    ": static. Rule: `rule.module.retired` `[Use-Removed]` (`spec/17` §1, D-0303). Invariant: none. Requ"
    "ired: the name used is live or deprecated. Observed: it is a tombstone, `[[removed(\"m\")]]`, or its m"
    "odule or its type is. Provenance: the use, and the tombstone. Repair: write what the message says in"
    "stead; no flag accepts a removed name. Related: `ex.removed-use`.\n- `diag.unittest-name` — Summary"
    ": this test's name cannot be used. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.unittest` `[Unittest-Name]` (`s"
    "pec/17` §6, D-0230). Invariant: none. Required: a `unittest`'s name, when it has one, is not empty,"
    " holds no control character, and is not the name of another test of the same module. Observed: an em"
    "pty name, a control character, or a second test of the module with that name. Provenance: the test a"
    "nd, for a repeated name, the first test with it. Repair: name each test of a module differently, say"
    " what it checks, or leave the name out. Location: the name.\n- `diag.type-mismatch` — Summary: the "
    "types do not match. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.type.typing` (any `[T-*]` premise failing), `[T-Conve"
    "rt]`, `[T-Alt]`, `[Limits-Not-Number]`, `[Print-Not-Printable]`, `[Append-Not-Printable]`, `[Parse-N"
    "ot-Numeric]`, `[Format-Arg-Mismatch]`, `[Key-Not-Hashable]`, `[Foreach-Not-Iterable]`, `[Foreach-Ran"
    "ge-Ill-Typed]`, `[Let-Destructure-Fields]`, `[Array-Repeat-Not-Plain]`. Required: the operand types "
