    " owned value, or restructure. Related: `ex.reference-escape`.\n- `diag.lifetime-elision-ambiguous` —"
    " Summary: it is not clear which parameter the returned reference comes from. Phase: static. Rule: `r"
    "ule.temporal.elision` `[Call-Multi-Ref-Return-Rejected]`. Required: exactly one reference parameter "
    "when returning a reference. Observed: zero or several. Provenance: the signature. Repair: one refere"
    "nce parameter, or return owned; `feat.explicit-lifetime-parameters` is the open general case. Relate"
    "d: `ex.lifetime-elision`.\n\n## Aliasing\n\n- `diag.aliasing-conflict` — Summary: this access conflict"
    "s with a live reference. Phase: both. Rule: `[Borrow-Denied]`, `[Read-Conflict]`, `[Write-Conflict]`"
    ", `[Match-Conflict]`, `[Thread-Affine]` (D-0213: an exclusive path of another running thread), `[Thr"
    "ead-Lend]` (a second lend of a live lent path). Invariant: `inv.alias-validity`, `inv.concurrency-va"
    "lidity`. Required: `¬clash(a, m)`. Observed: `witness(a, m, Σ)` — a live non-ancestor path with "
    "overlapping target and incompatible mode. Provenance: the witness's formation event (which borrow, i"
    "n which thread) vs. this access. Repair: end the conflicting reference (let its holder go out of sco"
    "pe) before this access, or use `shared` on both sides. Related: `ex.borrow-conflict`, `ex.projection"
    "-conflict`.\n- `diag.borrow-exceeds-source` — Summary: this reference would allow more than its sou"
    "rce does. Phase: static; dynamic for `[Read-Fn-Through-Shared]`. Rule: `[Borrow-Exceeds-Source]`, `["
    "T-Read-Through-Shared]` (an exclusive reference read through a shared one, where an exclusive one is"
    " expected), `[Read-Exclusive-Through-Shared]`, `[Match-Exclusive-Through-Shared]`, `[Read-Fn-Through"
    "-Shared]` (D-0218). Invariant: `inv.alias-validity`. Required: an exclusive borrow's source is exclu"
    "sive; nothing reached through a shared reference is used as a writer. Observed: source mode `shared`"
    "; a copy holding an exclusive reference; a closure with an exclusive capture. Provenance: the source"
    " reference's declared mode. Repair: take `ref<τ, exclusive>` where mutation is needed. Related: `ex"
    ".shared-is-read-only`.\n- `diag.write-through-shared` — Summary: this writes through a shared refer"
    "ence. Phase: static. Rule: `[Write-Not-Exclusive]` (a place reached through a shared path, including"
    " through an exclusive reference it holds: `[Read-Ref-Through-Shared]`, D-0218). Invariant: `inv.alia"
    "s-validity`. Required: `mode(a) = exclusive`. Observed: `shared`. Provenance: the path's mode at for"
    "mation. Repair: as above. Related: `ex.shared-is-read-only`.\n- `diag.destroy-while-aliased` — Summ"
    "ary: this is destroyed while a reference to it is live. Phase: both. Rule: `[Destroy-Not-Solitary]`."
    " Invariant: `inv.alias-validity`, `inv.temporal-validity`. Required: `solitary(a)`. Observed: anothe"
    "r live path (a reference, a guard). Provenance: that path's formation. Repair: let the reference's h"
    "older end first; release the guard. Related: `ex.destroy-while-borrowed`.\n- `diag.move-while-aliased"
    "` — Summary: this is moved while a reference to it is live. Phase: both. Rule: `[Authority-Transfe"
    "r-Aliased]`, `[Relocate-In-Aliased]`, `[Rawptr-Move-In]`/`-Out]` premises. Invariant: `inv.alias-val"
    "idity`. Required: no other live path on the moved object. Observed: one exists. Provenance: its form"
    "ation. Repair: end the reference before moving. Related: `ex.move-while-borrowed`.\n- `diag.move-out-"
    "of-field` — Summary: a part of a live value cannot be moved out on its own. Phase: static. Rule: `"
    "[Store-Binding-Place-Transfer-Sub]`, `[Destroy-Projection]`, `[Match-Move-Through-Ref]`, `[Let-Destr"
    "ucture-Destructor]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: a moved resource is a whole obje"
    "ct. Observed: a field/element/payload of a live object, or a payload reached through a reference. Pr"
    "ovenance: the projection. Repair: move the whole container, or take a reference to the field.\n- `dia"
    "g.borrow-of-non-place`, `diag.borrow-of-temporary` — Summary: only a place can be borrowed. Phase:"
    " static. Rule: `[Ref-Form-Not-Place]`, `[Ref-Form-Temporary]`; `[Simd-Lane]` (`spec/16` §3b, D-0254"
    "). Required: the operand of `&` is a place rooted in a binding, reference, or reclaim. Observed: a v"
    "alue or a temporary; a bit field; a lane of a `simd`, or a range of them. Repair: bind it first; rea"
    "d or assign the lane, or borrow the whole vector.\n\n## Resource authority\n\n- `diag.no-destroy-authori"
    "ty` — Summary: this code no longer owns the value it destroys. Phase: both. Rule: `[Destroy-No-Aut"
    "hority]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: unconsumed authority in this thread. Observ"
    "ed: absent (moved to another thread) or consumed. Provenance: the consuming/transferring event. Repa"
    "ir: destroy in the owning thread, once. (A second `drop(x)` through the same binding reports `diag.s"
    "tale-binding` first.) Related: `ex.double-destroy`.\n- `diag.transfer-without-authority` — Summary:"
    " this code no longer owns the value it hands on. Phase: both. Rule: `[Authority-Transfer-Unauthorize"
    "d]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`, `inv.temporal-validity`. Required: a valid source holding "
    "authority. Observed: stale or unauthorized. Provenance: the earlier move/destroy. Repair: move from "
    "the current holder. Related: `ex.use-after-move`.\n- `diag.overwrite-of-live-resource` — Summary: t"
    "his overwrites a resource that has not been ended. Phase: both. Rule: `[Write-Resource-Overwrite-Rej"
    "ected]`. Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: the target holds no live resource, or its ty"
    "pe is quiet (D-0194: then the write destroys it). Observed: an outstanding obligation at the target."
    " Provenance: the establishing/moving event that put it there. Repair: `overwrite(&mut place, v)` to "
    "put `v` there and destroy the old value (D-0080), `replace(&mut place, v)` to keep the old value, or"
    " `drop` the old value first. Related: `ex.no-silent-resource-overwrite`.\n- `diag.read-of-resource` —"
    " Summary: a resource cannot be copied by reading it. Phase: static. Rule: `[Read-Resource-Rejected]`"
    ". Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: `¬is-resource(type(a))` in value position. Observe"
    "d: resource. Provenance: the type declaration. Repair: move it, or take a reference. Related: `ex.no"
    "-copy-of-resource`.\n- `diag.destructor-on-plain-type` — Summary: only a resource can have a destru"
    "ctor. Phase: static. Rule: `spec/07` §1 (D-0075). Invariant: `inv.resource-authority`. Required: a "
    "type with a destructor is a resource in every instantiation. Observed: `T::drop` declared for a type"
    " that is not one. Provenance: the destructor's declaration. Repair: declare the type `resource struc"
    "t T` (or `resource enum T`).\n- `diag.bad-destructor-signature`, `diag.direct-destructor-call` — Su"
    "mmary: a destructor must be `T::drop(ref<T, exclusive> self)`, called only by `drop`. Phase: static."
    " Rule: `spec/07` §1. Required: `T::drop(ref<T, exclusive> self)`, invoked only by `[Destroy]`. Repa"
    "ir: fix the signature; use `drop(x)`.\n\n## Arithmetic\n\n- `diag.arith-overflow` — Summary: arithmeti"
    "c overflow. Phase: both. Rule: `[Arith-Checked-Overflow]`, `[Neg-Overflow]`. Invariant: `inv.arith.r"
    "ange-validity`. Required: `r ∈ represented-domain(τ)`. Observed: outside. Provenance: the operand"
    " values at this expression. Repair: widen, or use `wrapping_`/`saturating_`/`checked_`. Related: `ex"
    ".checked-arithmetic`, `ex.negation`.\n- `diag.div-by-zero` — Summary: division by zero. Phase: both"
    ". Rule: `[Div-By-Zero]`. Required: `v2 ≠ 0`. Repair: test first, or `checked_div`. Related: `ex.ch"
    "ecked-arithmetic`.\n- `diag.div-overflow` — Summary: division overflow: the minimum divided by -1. "
    "Phase: both. Rule: `[Div-Overflow]`. Required: `¬(v1 = min(τ) ∧ v2 = -1)`. Repair: `checked_div`"
    " or widen. Related: `ex.checked-arithmetic`.\n- `diag.shift-amount-out-of-range` — Summary: shift a"
    "mount out of range for the type. Phase: both. Rule: `[Shift-Amount-Invalid]`. Required: `0 ≤ n < b"
    "itwidth(τ)`. Repair: mask the amount.\n- `diag.narrowing-overflow` — Summary: the value does not f"
    "it the narrower type. Phase: both. Rule: `[Narrow-Overflow]`, `[Float-To-Int-Invalid]`, `[Bitfield-O"
    "verflow]` (`spec/16` §2a, D-0118). Required: `v ∈ represented-domain(τ')`. Repair: `narrow_wrapp"
    "ing`, or widen the target.\n- `diag.literal-out-of-range` — Summary: this literal does not fit its "
    "type. Phase: static. Rule: `[Literal-Out-Of-Range]`. Required: `val(L) ∈ represented-domain(τ)`; "
    "for a float literal, that it does not round beyond `τ`'s largest finite magnitude. Provenance: the "
    "literal vs. its determined type. Repair: fix the literal or annotation.\n\n## Aggregates\n\n- `diag.recu"
    "rsive-type` — Summary: this type contains itself. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.agg.layout` `[Type-Re"
    "cursive]` (`spec/16` §1). Invariant: none. Required: no struct or enum contains itself by value. Ob"
    "served: a chain of fields, payloads, array elements or `mutex` values leading back to the type, with"
    " no pointer on the way. Provenance: the type's declaration. Repair: put the recursive part behind a "
    "`Box<T>` (one owner), an `Rc<T>` (shared) or a `Vec<T>` (many). Location: the declaration.\n- `diag.s"
    "tatic-assert-failed` — Summary: static assertion failed. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.static-"
    "assert` `[Static-Assert-Failed]` (`spec/17` §1). Invariant: none. Required: the condition of `stati"
    "c_assert` is `true`. Observed: `false`, for the program as written or for one instantiation of a gen"
    "eric function (the message given, if any, is shown, formatted with its arguments' values). Provenanc"
    "e: the assertion and the constants and types it names. Repair: fix what the assertion guards, or the"
    " assertion. Location: the assertion.\n- `diag.static-assert-not-constant` — Summary: a static asser"
    "tion's condition must be known before the program runs. Phase: static. Rule: `rule.module.static-ass"
    "ert` `[Static-Assert-Not-Constant]` (`spec/17` §1b). Invariant: none. Required: the condition of `s"
    "tatic_assert` is a `bool` constant expression — literals, constants (module or local), operators, "
    "`sizeof`, `alignof`, the limits and the conversions — so that it can be computed before the progra"
    "m runs. Observed: the condition (or an argument of its message) names a local variable or parameter,"
    " calls a function or reads a container, or the condition is not a `bool`. Provenance: the condition."
    " Repair: for a condition that is only known when the program runs, use `assert` (`spec/18` §1a); to"
    " check a value before the program runs, name it with `const` (a local `const` works: `const u8 D = B"
    " + 1;`). Location: the assertion.\n- `diag.not-char-boundary` — Summary: this bound falls inside a "
    "character. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.stringview` `[View-Boundary]` (`spec/21` §2h). Invari"
    "ant: `inv.string.utf8-validity`. Required: both bounds of a `StringView` fall at the start of a char"
    "acter or at the end of the text. Observed: a bound inside a character's UTF-8 encoding. Provenance: "
    "the view's bounds. Repair: move the bound to a character's start (a byte that is not `0b10xxxxxx`), "
    "for example by searching with `StringView::find`. Location: the view.\n- `diag.invalid-datetime` — "
    "Summary: this date and time do not exist. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.time` `[Invalid-DateTim"
    "e]` (`spec/21` §2j, D-0140). Invariant: none. Required: the `DateTime` names a moment of the prolep"
    "tic Gregorian calendar (a month 1 to 12, a day within its month, an hour below 24, a minute and a se"
    "cond below 60) at most `i64` seconds from 1970. Observed: a field out of range, or a year too far fr"
    "om 1970. Provenance: the `DateTime`, written as a struct literal or with its fields changed. Repair:"
    " make it with `DateTime::new`, which returns `None` for such fields, or with `DateTime::from_unix`/`"
    "from_iso`. Location: the call of `DateTime::to_unix` (or `weekday`).\n- `diag.entropy-unavailable` —"
    " Summary: the operating system gave no secure random bytes. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §0 `[Os"
    "-Random]` (D-0142). Invariant: none. Required: the operating system gives bytes from its cryptograph"
    "ically secure source. Observed: it has none, or refused (on Linux, no `getrandom` and no readable `/"
    "dev/urandom`, as in a bare container). Provenance: the call. Repair: run where the system provides s"
    "ecure randomness; never substitute a clock or a fixed seed for keys. Location: the call of `os_rando"
    "m_bytes`, `os_random_u64` or `Rng::from_os`.\n- `diag.hkdf-length` — Summary: HKDF cannot produce m"
    "ore than 8160 bytes. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §2m `[Hkdf]` (D-0152). Invariant: none. Requir"
    "ed: `hkdf_expand`'s `len` is at most 8160, 255 blocks of 32 bytes (RFC 5869's bound). Observed: a la"
    "rger `len`. Provenance: the call. Repair: derive at most 8160 bytes from one pseudorandom key; deriv"
    "e more keys with different `info`. Location: the call of `hkdf_expand` or `hkdf_sha256`.\n- `diag.cry"
    "pto-length` — Summary: a key, nonce or digest of the wrong length. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21`"
    " §2m `[Crypto-Length]` (D-0153, D-0154, D-0165, D-0167, D-0168, D-0169, D-0170). Invariant: none. R"
    "equired: a ChaCha20 or AEAD key of 32 bytes and a nonce of 12, an AES key of 16, 24 or 32 bytes and "
    "an AES-GCM nonce of 12 (D-0165), an X25519, P-256 or Ed25519 private key of 32 bytes and a P-384 pri"
    "vate key of 48, a Poly1305 key of 32 bytes, a ChaCha20 message that fits in the 2^32 blocks after it"
    "s starting counter, a BLAKE2b digest of 1 to 64 bytes under a key of at most 64, an RSA digest of it"
    "s hash's length and a modulus long enough for the signature encoding, and an RSA key size of 1024 to"
    " 8192 bits in a multiple of 64. Observed: another length. Provenance: the call. Repair: pass keys an"
    "d nonces of the algorithm's sizes (a key from `hkdf_expand` with `len` 32, a nonce of 12 bytes, a di"
    "gest from `hash` of the `HashKind` named). Location: the call into `std::crypto`.\n- `diag.kdf-parame"
    "ters` — Summary: the key-derivation parameters are out of range. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §"
    "2m `[Kdf-Parameters]` (D-0170). Invariant: none. Required: `pbkdf2` runs at least one iteration; `ar"
    "gon2id` (and a PHC string `verify_password` reads, which is false instead) has at least one pass, 1 "
    "to 255 lanes, at least 8 KiB of memory per lane, a salt of at least 8 bytes and a result of at least"
    " 4 bytes (RFC 9106 §3.1). Observed: a parameter outside those bounds. Provenance: the call. Repair:"
    " pass the parameters the standard allows; `hash_password` chooses them itself. Location: the call of"
    " `pbkdf2` or `argon2id`.\n- `diag.not-ascii` — Summary: this byte is not ASCII. Phase: dynamic. Rul"
    "e: `rule.stdlib.text` `[Push-Ascii-Not-Ascii]` (`spec/21` §2d). Invariant: `inv.string.utf8-validit"
    "y`. Required: the byte given to `String::push_ascii` is below 128. Observed: a byte of 128 or more, "
    "which is not UTF-8 on its own. Provenance: the call. Repair: build bytes in a `Vec<u8>` and check th"
    "em with `String::from_utf8`. Location: the call.\n- `diag.index-out-of-bounds` — Summary: index out"
    " of bounds. Phase: both. Rule: `[Index-Out-Of-Bounds]`, `[Slice-Out-Of-Bounds]` (`spec/16` §3a), `s"
    "pec/21` §1 `fault`, `[Str-Byte-Out-Of-Bounds]` (`spec/21` §2a), `arg`'s `fault` (`spec/21` §2c). "
    "Invariant: `inv.spatial-validity`. Required: `0 ≤ n < N` / `i < len` / `i < str_len(s)` / `i < arg"
    "_count()`. Observed: violated. Provenance: the index value vs. the fixed `N`, current `len`, the `st"
    "r`'s byte count, or the number of arguments. Repair: check first, or use `pop`/`checked` accessors. "
    "Related: `ex.bounds-check`, `ex.str-literal`.\n- `diag.non-exhaustive-match` — Summary: this `match"
    "` does not cover every value. Phase: static. Rule: `[Match-Non-Exhaustive]`. Required: the arms toge"
    "ther match every value (every variant, at every level a pattern descends to, or `_`). Observed: a pa"
    "ttern no arm matches, given as the message. Provenance: the enum declarations vs. the arms. Repair: "
    "add an arm for the pattern named, or a `_` arm. Related: `ex.exhaustive-match`.\n- `diag.unreachable-"
    "arm` — Summary: this arm can never be reached. Phase: static. Rule: `[Match-Unreachable]`. Require"
    "d: each arm matches some value no earlier arm matches (arms are tried in order). Observed: an arm ev"
    "ery value of which an earlier arm takes. Provenance: the arm vs. the earlier arms. Repair: remove th"
    "e arm, or move it before the arm that takes its values.\n\n## Failure, concurrency, trust\n\n- `diag.pro"
    "pagate-outside-fallible-context` — Summary: `?` cannot be used in this function. Phase: static. Ru"
    "le: `[Propagate-Err-Mismatch]`, `[Propagate-Option-Mismatch]` (D-0130). Required: the function retur"
    "ns `Result<_, E>` with matching `E` (for a `Result` operand), or an `Option` (for an `Option` operan"
    "d). Provenance: the declared return type vs. the `?` site. Repair: change the return type, `Result::"
    "map_err`, `Option::ok_or(o, e)?` (an `Option` in a `Result`-returning function), or `match`.\n- `diag"
    ".spawn-borrow-closure` — Summary: a spawned thread needs a `move` closure. Phase: static. Rule: `r"
    "ule.conc.spawn`. Required: a `fn` value or `move` closure. Repair: add `move`.\n- `diag.mutex-reentra"
    "nt-lock` — Summary: this thread already holds the lock. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `[Lock-Reentrant]`. "
    "Invariant: `inv.concurrency-validity`. Required: the thread does not already hold the lock. Provenan"
    "ce: the live guard. Repair: release the guard first.\n- `diag.trusted-outside-unsafe` — Summary: th"
    "is needs an `unsafe` block. Phase: static. Rule: `[Unsafe-Rejected]`. Invariant: `inv.trust-transiti"
    "on`. Required: every trusted construct inside `unsafe { }`. Provenance: the construct vs. the neares"
    "t enclosing `unsafe`. Repair: wrap in `unsafe` after verifying the asserted property. Related: `ex.u"
    "nsafe-required`.\n- `diag.extern-non-ffi-type` — Summary: this type cannot cross into C. Phase: sta"
    "tic. Rule: `[Extern-Non-Ffi-Type]`. Required: `FfiType` parameters and result: integers, `f32`, `f64"
    "`, `bool`, `void` (a result), `rawptr<τ>`, and plain structs of those (`ffi-struct`, D-0252). Obser"
    "ved: the first type that is none of these, named through the field path that reaches it. Repair: pas"
    "s `rawptr`/scalars, or a struct without resources, enums or bitstructs.\n- `diag.null-pointer` — Su"
    "mmary: C's `NULL` where text was expected. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.stdlib.ffi` `[From-C-Null]` ("
    "`spec/21` §3f, D-0252). Invariant: none. Required: the `rawptr<u8>` given to `String::from_c` or `V"
    "ec::from_c_bytes` is not `null_rawptr<u8>()`. Observed: address 0. Provenance: the C function that r"
    "eturned it. Repair: test with `is_null` first; C functions return `NULL` for \"none\". Location: the c"
    "all.\n- `diag.assert-failed` — Summary: assertion failed. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.fail.assert` "
    "`[Assert-Fail]` (`spec/18` §1a). Invariant: none. Required: the condition of `assert` is `true`. Ob"
    "served: `false` (the message the program gave, if any, formatted, is shown after the location). Prov"
    "enance: the call. Repair: the program's own condition names what was assumed; find why it did not ho"
    "ld. Location: the call.\n- `diag.channel-zero-capacity` — Summary: a channel needs a capacity of at"
    " least 1. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.conc.channel` `[Channel-Zero-Capacity]` (`spec/19` §3). Invar"
    "iant: none. Required: the capacity given to `Channel::new` is at least 1. Observed: 0. Provenance: t"
    "he call. Repair: give the number of values the channel may hold; 1 for a hand-over. Location: the ca"
    "ll.\n- `diag.barrier-zero-parties` — Summary: a barrier needs at least one party. Phase: dynamic. R"
    "ule: `rule.stdlib.waiting` `[Barrier-Zero-Parties]` (`spec/21` §3c‴). Invariant: none. Required: "
    "the number of parties given to `Barrier::new` is at least 1. Observed: 0. Provenance: the call. Repa"
    "ir: give the number of threads that meet at the barrier. Location: the call.\n- `diag.channel-deadloc"
    "k` — Summary: the only running thread waits on a channel nothing else can change. Phase: dynamic. "
    "Rule: `rule.conc.channel` `[Channel-Deadlock]` (`spec/19` §3). Invariant: none. Required: while `Ch"
    "annel::send` or `Channel::recv` waits, another thread exists that could change the channel. Observed"
    ": the program's only running thread waits on a full or empty channel that is not closed. Provenance:"
    " the call. Repair: send or receive from another thread, or `close` the channel before receiving the "
    "last value. Location: the call.\n- `diag.thread-cancelled` — Summary: this thread was cancelled. Ph"
    "ase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.conc.cancel` `[Cancel]` (`spec/19` §1, D-0204). Invariant: none. Required"
    ": the thread was not asked to stop while it waits. Observed: `cancel` was called on its handle; it w"
    "as waiting (a join, a lock, a channel, sleeping, a socket) or began to. Provenance: the `cancel` cal"
    "l. Repair: none is needed when the stop was meant: the thread's failure is contained, and its joiner"
    " or handle sees it; to let a thread finish, do not cancel it. Location: the wait.\n- `diag.mutex-pois"
    "oned` — Summary: a thread failed while holding this lock. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `rule.conc.lock` `"
    "[Lock-Poisoned]` (`spec/19` §2, D-0204). Invariant: `inv.concurrency-validity`. Required: the mutex"
    " was not held by a thread whose fault was contained. Observed: such a thread held it when it failed,"
    " so its interior may be half-changed. Provenance: the failed thread's fault. Repair: find that fault"
    " (`try_join` gives it); keep a lock's block short, so that little can fail inside it. Location: the "
    "`lock`.\n- `diag.deadlock` — Summary: these threads would wait for each other forever. Phase: dynam"
    "ic. Rule: `rule.conc.guarantee` `[Deadlock]` (`spec/19` §4, D-0204). Invariant: none. Required: the"
    " wait can end. Observed: waiting would close a cycle of threads waiting to join or lock each other's"
    ", or every thread waits on another, a mutex, a channel or an atomic (`Atomic::wait`, D-0253), and no"
    "ne on the clock or outside the program. Provenance: the waits. Repair: take locks in one order; send"
    " before waiting to receive; store and notify before waiting on an atomic another thread waits to see"
    " change; join a thread only after giving it what it waits for. Location: the wait.\n- `diag.result-di"
    "scarded` — Summary: a `Result` is discarded. Phase: static. Rule: `spec/13` §3 `[Stmt-Result-Disc"
    "arded]` (D-0099). Invariant: none. Required: a statement's value that is a `Result` is used — prop"
    "agated with `?`, matched, bound, passed or returned. Observed: an expression statement (or a block-l"
    "ike statement) whose value is a `Result`, discarded. Provenance: the statement. Repair: handle the e"
    "rror (`?`, `match`), or discard the value on purpose with `_ = e;`.\n- `diag.stack-exhausted` — Sum"
    "mary: calls nested too deeply for the stack. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/15` §3 `[Call-Stack-Exhaus"
    "ted]` (D-0077). Invariant: none (an implementation limit). Required: the implementation can give the"
    " call a frame. Observed: calls nested deeper than the stack the implementation provides. Provenance:"
    " the call. Repair: recurse less deeply (a loop, an explicit stack in a `Vec`).\n- `diag.unwrap-failed"
    "` — Summary: nothing to unwrap: `None` or `Err`. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §1 `Option::unwr"
    "ap`, `Option::expect`, `Result::unwrap`, `Result::expect` (D-0082). Invariant: none. Required: the `"
    "Option` is `Some`, the `Result` is `Ok`. Observed: `None` or `Err` (`expect`'s message, or which cal"
    "l it was, is shown after the location). Provenance: the call. Repair: match on the value, or give a "
    "default with `unwrap_or`, where its absence is possible. Location: the call.\n- `diag.alloc-failure` "
    "— Summary: memory could not be allocated. Phase: dynamic. Rule: `spec/21` §1/§3 `fault(alloc_fai"
    "lure)` after `allocate` returns `Err`. Required: allocation succeeded. Provenance: the `allocate` ca"
    "ll. Repair: none at the language level; callers needing recovery call `allocate` themselves.\n\n## Cha"
    "nge Log\n\n- 1.62.0 — `CHG-0401` (D-0303): `diag.deprecated-use` and `diag.removed-use`.\n- 1.61.0 —"
